                <pb facs="0655" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.73/158: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Riddle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-11T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:16 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Department’s 34, August 7, 4 p.m. Minister for Foreign Affairs today informed
                    me that in view of Western Company’s renunciation, <pb facs="0656" n="536"
                        xml:id="pg536"/> the Argentine Government does not consider that contract
                    constitutes an obstacle to granting equal privileges to an American company and
                    he promised me early written note in confirmation. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Riddle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
